 - [ ] **PREVIEW-003**: When concurrent requests miss the cache for the same preview key, the system SHALL return 202 with the same job ticket and a two-second retry interval while one shared render job is pending.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed 12 GiB of cached JPEG data, the system SHALL evict entries before admission so the cache remains within that limit.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-005**: When a render job fails, the system SHALL release its deduplication entry so a later request can enqueue a new job.
+
+## Cache Replacement
+
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-006**: When the preview worker admits a newly rendered contact sheet whose preview key is not recorded in the ghost queue, the system SHALL place the sheet in the first-use queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-007**: When a contact sheet held in the first-use queue is retrieved from the cache and that retrieval is not the sheet's delivery, the system SHALL move the sheet to the hot queue without re-rendering it.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-008**: When a contact sheet held in the hot queue is retrieved from the cache, the system SHALL refresh the sheet's position within the hot queue without re-rendering it.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-009**: When a contact sheet is evicted from the hot queue, the system SHALL record the sheet's preview key in the ghost queue and SHALL NOT retain the sheet's JPEG data.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-010**: When a requested preview key is recorded in the ghost queue, the system SHALL render the sheet again, SHALL admit the rendered sheet directly to the hot queue, and SHALL remove the preview key from the ghost queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-011**: When admitting a contact sheet to the first-use queue would exceed the first-use byte budget, the system SHALL evict first-use-queue sheets in admission order until the sheet can be admitted.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-012**: When admitting a contact sheet to the hot queue would exceed the hot byte budget, the system SHALL evict hot-queue sheets in least-recently-retrieved order until the sheet can be admitted.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-013**: The system SHALL partition the 12 GiB cached-JPEG budget into a first-use byte budget and a hot byte budget whose sum is 12 GiB.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-014**: When a contact sheet is admitted to the cache, the system SHALL treat the first subsequent retrieval of that sheet as its delivery and SHALL NOT count that retrieval as reuse.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-016**: When multiple render jobs complete concurrently, the system SHALL serialize admission so that cached JPEG data never exceeds 12 GiB.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-017**: The system SHALL retain at most 4,096 preview keys in the ghost queue and SHALL discard the oldest recorded key when the ghost queue is full.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-018**: When a contact sheet's size exceeds the first-use byte budget, the system SHALL admit the sheet to the hot queue instead; and when its size exceeds the hot byte budget, the system SHALL serve the sheet without caching it.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-019**: The system SHALL hold a preview key in at most one of the first-use queue, the hot queue, and the ghost queue at any time.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-020**: The system SHALL key every cached preview by clip ID, clip revision, and renderer version.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-021**: The system SHALL keep temporary render output separate from cached JPEG data and SHALL remove that output when the render job completes or fails.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-022**: The system SHALL run at most four render jobs concurrently.
+
+## Internal Boundaries
+
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-015**: The internal preview endpoint SHALL return only 200, 202, or 404 and SHALL NOT expose cache queue membership, eviction counters, or replacement-policy configuration.
